From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mhc: fp32 TileLang prenorm GEMM at every T

VLLM_GLM5_TARGET_PRENORM_FP32 (default 0; the _0026 suffix is the
development number, kept so existing deployments keep working). Our mHC
prenorm GEMM takes a bf16 cuBLAS route for some token counts (e.g. the
T=32 verify batch), Morrowmake never does: its prenorm is an fp32-FMA
TileLang kernel at every T. With the switch the same dispatch is used
(T<128: n_thr 1024 / tile_n 4; T<1024: 512 / 12; else block_m 2), so mixes
are fp32 from fp32 fn. Covers prefill, decode M>16 and the PP receiver's
standalone hc_pre. Together with VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_MHC_V2 (0017) the first
block of an identical history matches the reference bit for bit, and the
prose acceptance gap closes.

diff --git a/vllm/model_executor/kernels/mhc/tilelang.py b/vllm/model_executor/kernels/mhc/tilelang.py
index 102d216..5127763 100644
--- a/vllm/model_executor/kernels/mhc/tilelang.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/kernels/mhc/tilelang.py
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
+import os
+
 import torch
 
 import vllm.envs as envs
@@ -93,6 +95,36 @@ def _tilelang_hc_prenorm_gemm(
         _torch_hc_prenorm_gemm(x, fn, out, sqrsum)
         return
     use_default_config = tile_n == 12 and n_thr == 512
+    if (
+        n_splits == 1
+        and use_default_config
+        and os.environ.get("VLLM_GLM5_TARGET_PRENORM_FP32", "0") == "1"
+    ):
+        # Target prenorm in fp32 (VLLM_GLM5_TARGET_PRENORM_FP32, default
+        # off; enable together with VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_MHC_V2). The reference
+        # (Morrowmake) has no bf16 cuBLAS route: its prenorm GEMM is
+        # an fp32-FMA TileLang kernel at every T (HcPrenormGemmTileLangKernel
+        # .dispatch: T<128 -> (n_thr 1024, tile_n 4); T<1024 -> (512, 12);
+        # else block_m=2, tile_n=12). Mirror that exact dispatch so `mixes`
+        # are fp32 from fp32 `fn`, never bf16(fn) with a bf16-rounded output.
+        # Covers prefill, decode M>16, and the PP receiver's standalone hc_pre.
+        hc_hidden = x.shape[1]
+        if x.shape[0] >= 1024:
+            hc_prenorm_gemm_block_m_tilelang(
+                x, fn, out, sqrsum, hidden_size, hc_mult, fn.shape[0],
+                512, 12, 2,
+            )
+        elif x.shape[0] < 128 and hc_hidden % 1024 == 0:
+            hc_prenorm_gemm_tilelang(
+                x, fn, out, sqrsum, hidden_size, hc_mult, fn.shape[0],
+                1024, 4, 1,
+            )
+        else:
+            hc_prenorm_gemm_tilelang(
+                x, fn, out, sqrsum, hidden_size, hc_mult, fn.shape[0],
+                512, 12, 1,
+            )
+        return
     if (
         n_splits == 1
         and use_default_config
